Make dynamic shared memory work in a single address space.

`dynamic_shared_memory_type` cannot be turned off -- PostgreSQL 12 removed the
`none` setting, and every EXEC_BACKEND child attaches the control segment
during startup -- so it has to work before a postmaster can run at all.

Upstream backs each segment with a file and maps it MAP_SHARED. Unikraft
supports MAP_SHARED for anonymous mappings only, so that fails; mapping the
file MAP_PRIVATE instead appears to work and then hands each process its own
private copy, which shows up one step later as

  FATAL:  dynamic shared memory control segment is not valid

Since every process shares one page table, an anonymous mapping is already
visible to all of them at the same address. This rewrite demotes the file from
storage to a name: it records the address and length of an anonymous mapping,
and attaching becomes a lookup.

--- a/src/backend/storage/ipc/dsm_impl.c
+++ b/src/backend/storage/ipc/dsm_impl.c
@@ -793,6 +793,46 @@
 			  void **impl_private, void **mapped_address, Size *mapped_size,
